import{_ as t,a,c as i,j as r}from"./chunks/framework.DVzkjf-b.js";const h=JSON.parse('{"title":"MetaVis — Engineering AI Through Evidence and Evaluation","description":"A source-linked case study of Swift, Metal, deterministic media tests, Gemini qualitative QA, and bounded AI feedback.","frontmatter":{"title":"MetaVis — Engineering AI Through Evidence and Evaluation","description":"A source-linked case study of Swift, Metal, deterministic media tests, Gemini qualitative QA, and bounded AI feedback."},"headers":[],"relativePath":"research/systems/metavis-evidence-and-evaluation.md","filePath":"research/systems/metavis-evidence-and-evaluation.md"}'),s={name:"research/systems/metavis-evidence-and-evaluation.md"};function n(o,e,c,d,l,m){return a(),i("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[r('<h1 id="metavis-engineering-ai-through-evidence-and-evaluation" tabindex="-1">MetaVis: Engineering AI Through Evidence and Evaluation <a class="header-anchor" href="#metavis-engineering-ai-through-evidence-and-evaluation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;MetaVis: Engineering AI Through Evidence and Evaluation&quot;">​</a></h1><p><em>Technical case study · December 2025 experiments, reviewed November 2026</em></p><p><strong>MetaVis was an exploration of how AI can direct sophisticated software while tests and specialized hardware establish measurable constraints.</strong> It was not only a video editor prototype; the tests themselves were experimental instruments.</p><h2 id="architecture" tabindex="-1">Architecture <a class="header-anchor" href="#architecture" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Architecture&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The <a href="https://github.com/kaw393939/metavis-demo-projects/blob/main/Package.swift" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">SwiftPM workspace</a> separates timeline models, a compiler, Metal rendering, native media ingestion, perception, export, session orchestration, and quality control. The design expresses high-level editing intent as a typed timeline and compiles it into a precise render graph. AI can propose editing actions; deterministic code performs them.</p><p>The <a href="https://github.com/kaw393939/metavis-demo-projects/blob/main/Docs/CONCEPT_VIBE_EDITING.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">vibe-editing design</a> calls for grounded context, typed intents, deterministic commands, reversibility, and test-locked semantics. The architecture also records where abstraction can become costly: the <a href="https://github.com/kaw393939/metavis-demo-projects/blob/main/Docs/SYSTEM_CRITIQUE.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">system critique</a> warns against using stateful-device interfaces for every operation in a real-time rendering loop.</p><h2 id="tests-as-instruments-not-decoration" tabindex="-1">Tests as instruments, not decoration <a class="header-anchor" href="#tests-as-instruments-not-decoration" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Tests as instruments, not decoration&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The <a href="https://github.com/kaw393939/metavis-demo-projects/blob/main/Docs/TDD_STRATEGY.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">TDD strategy</a> calls for protocols, dependency injection, golden fixtures, and layered tests.</p><p>Examples in the source:</p><ul><li><a href="https://github.com/kaw393939/metavis-demo-projects/blob/main/Tests/MetaVisSimulationTests/Golden/GoldenFrameHashTests.swift" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Golden frame hashes</a>: render procedural test patterns and check stable downsampled hashes.</li><li><a href="https://github.com/kaw393939/metavis-demo-projects/blob/main/Tests/MetaVisSimulationTests/TwinVerificationTests.swift" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">CPU/GPU twin comparison</a>: compare a Metal path to a reference buffer.</li><li><a href="https://github.com/kaw393939/metavis-demo-projects/blob/main/Tests/MetaVisPerceptionTests/MasterSensorsDeterminismTests.swift" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Sensor determinism</a>: ingest the same media twice and assert identical structured sensor results.</li><li><a href="https://github.com/kaw393939/metavis-demo-projects/blob/main/Tests/MetaVisSimulationTests/Perf/RenderAllocationTests.swift" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Allocation invariants</a>: after warm-up, repeated frames should not allocate new Metal textures.</li><li><a href="https://github.com/kaw393939/metavis-demo-projects/blob/main/Tests/MetaVisExportTests/DeliverableE2ETests.swift" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Export contracts</a>: verify media, manifests, sidecars, quality reports, and absence of normal-path CPU readback.</li></ul><p>These tests encode not only functionality but resource constraints. A video can look correct while missing an audio track, rendering the wrong content for seconds, or performing costly texture allocations.</p><h2 id="deterministic-measures-and-qualitative-gemini-review" tabindex="-1">Deterministic measures and qualitative Gemini review <a class="header-anchor" href="#deterministic-measures-and-qualitative-gemini-review" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Deterministic measures and qualitative Gemini review&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The <a href="https://github.com/kaw393939/metavis-demo-projects/blob/main/Sources/MetaVisQC/VideoQC.swift" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">VideoQC</a> and <a href="https://github.com/kaw393939/metavis-demo-projects/blob/main/Sources/MetaVisQC/VideoContentQC.swift" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">VideoContentQC</a> modules measure frame counts, codec-related properties, silence, temporal variety, and image statistics.</p><p>The optional <a href="https://github.com/kaw393939/metavis-demo-projects/blob/main/Sources/MetaVisQC/GeminiQC.swift" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GeminiQC</a> layer adds qualitative judgments. Its <a href="https://github.com/kaw393939/metavis-demo-projects/blob/main/Sources/MetaVisQC/GeminiPromptBuilder.swift" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">prompt builder</a> supplies expected narrative and deterministic metrics, limits external media according to privacy policies, and requests structured responses.</p><p>More importantly, the <a href="https://github.com/kaw393939/metavis-demo-projects/blob/main/Sprints/16_Feedback_done/archive/PLAN.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Sprint 16 feedback loop</a> creates a <strong>budgeted EvidencePack</strong> from selected frames, short audio/video snippets, and sensor summaries. It can ask for targeted additional evidence rather than upload entire deliverables. <a href="https://github.com/kaw393939/metavis-demo-projects/blob/main/Sources/MetaVisLab/AutoColorCorrectQA.swift" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">AutoColorCorrectQA</a> provides a numeric exposure heuristic, while permitting a Gemini reviewer to disagree if actual visual evidence justifies it. A <a href="https://github.com/kaw393939/metavis-demo-projects/blob/main/Sources/MetaVisCore/FeedbackLoopContracts.swift" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">ParameterWhitelist</a> enforces bounded edits in code.</p><p>The AI reviewer supplies judgments and proposed changes; it does <strong>not</strong> replace measured physical constraints.</p><h2 id="hardware-optimization-as-an-engineering-boundary" tabindex="-1">Hardware optimization as an engineering boundary <a class="header-anchor" href="#hardware-optimization-as-an-engineering-boundary" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Hardware optimization as an engineering boundary&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The <a href="https://github.com/kaw393939/metavis-demo-projects/blob/main/Docs/CONCEPT_HARDWARE_MAXIMIZATION.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">hardware maximization design</a> assigns suitable workloads to Apple media engines, Core ML/Vision, and Metal, while limiting copies and reusing buffers. The <a href="https://github.com/kaw393939/metavis-demo-projects/blob/main/Sprints/24i_shader_perf_m3/FINDINGS.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">performance findings</a> record measurements on an Apple M3 machine dated December 22–23, 2025. These are engineering observations, not controlled comparative performance claims.</p><h2 id="gaps-and-research-implications" tabindex="-1">Gaps and research implications <a class="header-anchor" href="#gaps-and-research-implications" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Gaps and research implications&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The repository includes examples of genuine self-critique. A <a href="https://github.com/kaw393939/metavis-demo-projects/blob/main/Docs/code_review/Master_Executive_Summary.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">December 21 AI code audit</a> identifies mock services and incomplete production AI pathways. Some real-asset fixtures are not tracked publicly, some tests require optional environment gates, and some AI-QA skip paths report acceptance rather than distinguishing <em>not run</em> from <em>passed</em>. AI judgments also need independent human calibration.</p><p>These limitations are particularly instructive. The evaluation harness itself requires governance, data provenance, and auditability.</p><p><strong>Generalizable hypothesis:</strong> a layered evaluation system—deterministic measurement, selected evidence, constrained probabilistic critique, bounded revision, then authorized review—can produce more trustworthy artifacts while spending fewer expensive evaluation resources.</p><p><a href="./">Research series</a> · <a href="./human-attention-kanban">Human attention and Kanban</a></p>',23)])])}const u=t(s,[["render",n]]);export{h as __pageData,u as default};
